*----------------------------------------------------------------------*
* SAP Gateway Service Builder (SEGW) Configuration
* Service: Z_INSPECTION_SRV
*
* This document describes how the OData service would be configured
* in SAP Gateway (transaction SEGW), equivalent to:
*   - srv/inspection-service.cds (service definition)
*   - The auto-generated OData endpoints from CAP
*----------------------------------------------------------------------*

======================================================================
1. SERVICE PROJECT
======================================================================
  Project Name:        Z_INSPECTION_SRV
  Project Description: Quality Inspection OData Service
  Package:             ZQUALITY_INSPECTION
  OData Version:       V4 (via SAP Gateway V4 or RAP)
  Generation Strategy: Reference to CDS View (preferred for S/4HANA)

  Generated Classes:
    MPC (Model Provider):  ZCL_Z_INSPECTION_SRV_MPC
    DPC (Data Provider):   ZCL_Z_INSPECTION_SRV_DPC

======================================================================
2. ENTITY TYPES
======================================================================

--- Entity Type: Inspection ---
  Properties:
    InspectionLotID    Edm.String(12)   [Key]
    MaterialNumber     Edm.String(20)
    MaterialDescription Edm.String(100)
    Plant              Edm.String(4)
    InspectionType     Edm.String(40)
    Status             Edm.String(20)
    CreatedDate        Edm.DateTime
    Inspector          Edm.String(80)
    Quantity           Edm.Int32
    UnitOfMeasure      Edm.String(4)
    BatchNumber        Edm.String(20)
    UsageDecisionCode  Edm.String(10)
    UsageDecisionDate  Edm.DateTime

  CRUD Operations:
    CREATE  → ZCL_Z_INSPECTION_SRV_DPC~INSPECTIONSET_CREATE_ENTITY
    READ    → ZCL_Z_INSPECTION_SRV_DPC~INSPECTIONSET_GET_ENTITY
    UPDATE  → ZCL_Z_INSPECTION_SRV_DPC~INSPECTIONSET_UPDATE_ENTITY
    DELETE  → ZCL_Z_INSPECTION_SRV_DPC~INSPECTIONSET_DELETE_ENTITY
    QUERY   → ZCL_Z_INSPECTION_SRV_DPC~INSPECTIONSET_GET_ENTITYSET

  Bound Action (Function Import):
    Name:           RecordUsageDecision
    HTTP Method:    POST
    Return Type:    Inspection
    Parameters:
      InspectionLotID   Edm.String(12)   [Bound Entity Key]
      Decision          Edm.String(10)   [Input: "Accept" or "Reject"]
    Implementation: ZCL_Z_INSPECTION_SRV_DPC~RECORD_USAGE_DECISION
    Equivalent CAP: action recordUsageDecision(decision : String(10)) returns Inspections;


--- Entity Type: InspectionResult ---
  Properties:
    ResultID           Edm.String(10)   [Key]
    InspectionLotID    Edm.String(12)   [FK → Inspection]
    CharacteristicName Edm.String(80)
    TargetValue        Edm.String(20)
    ActualValue        Edm.String(20)
    Unit               Edm.String(20)
    Tolerance          Edm.String(20)
    Valuation          Edm.String(10)

  CRUD Operations:
    READ    → ZCL_Z_INSPECTION_SRV_DPC~INSPRESULTSET_GET_ENTITY
    QUERY   → ZCL_Z_INSPECTION_SRV_DPC~INSPRESULTSET_GET_ENTITYSET


======================================================================
3. ENTITY SETS
======================================================================
  InspectionSet        → Entity Type: Inspection
  InspectionResultSet  → Entity Type: InspectionResult


======================================================================
4. NAVIGATION PROPERTIES
======================================================================
  Inspection → InspectionResultSet
    Name:           ToResults
    Relationship:   InspToResult
    From Role:      InspectionLot
    To Role:        InspectionResult
    Cardinality:    1..N
    FK:             InspectionLotID → InspectionLotID

  Equivalent in CAP:
    Composition of many InspectionResults on Results.inspection = $self

  URL pattern:
    /sap/opu/odata/sap/Z_INSPECTION_SRV/InspectionSet('100000001')/ToResults
    ↔ CAP: /odata/v4/InspectionService/Inspections('100000001')?$expand=Results


======================================================================
5. SERVICE REGISTRATION & ACTIVATION
======================================================================

  Step 1: Generate Runtime Artifacts (in SEGW)
    - Menu → Generate → will create MPC + DPC classes

  Step 2: Register Service (transaction /IWFND/MAINT_SERVICE)
    - Technical Service Name: Z_INSPECTION_SRV
    - System Alias: LOCAL
    - ICF Node: /sap/opu/odata/sap/Z_INSPECTION_SRV

  Step 3: Test in SAP Gateway Client (transaction /IWFND/GW_CLIENT)
    - $metadata:  /sap/opu/odata/sap/Z_INSPECTION_SRV/$metadata
    - Entity Set: /sap/opu/odata/sap/Z_INSPECTION_SRV/InspectionSet
    - Single:     /sap/opu/odata/sap/Z_INSPECTION_SRV/InspectionSet('100000001')
    - Expand:     /sap/opu/odata/sap/Z_INSPECTION_SRV/InspectionSet('100000001')?$expand=ToResults


======================================================================
6. ALTERNATIVE: RAP (ABAP RESTful Application Programming Model)
======================================================================

  In S/4HANA (ABAP Cloud), the preferred approach is RAP:

  -- Behavior Definition --
  managed implementation in class ZBP_INSPECTION unique;

  define behavior for Z_INSPECTION_LOT alias Inspection
  persistent table QALS
  lock master
  {
    create;
    update;
    delete;

    field ( readonly ) InspectionLotID;
    field ( mandatory ) MaterialNumber, Plant;

    determination GenerateLotID on save { create; }
    validation ValidateStatusTransition on save { update; }

    action recordUsageDecision parameter ZS_USAGE_DECISION result [1] $self;

    association _Results { create; }
  }

  define behavior for Z_INSPECTION_RESULT alias Result
  persistent table QASE
  lock dependent by _InspectionLot
  {
    update;
    delete;

    field ( readonly ) ResultID;

    association _InspectionLot;
  }

  -- Service Definition --
  define service Z_INSPECTION_API {
    expose Z_INSPECTION_LOT as Inspections;
    expose Z_INSPECTION_RESULT as InspectionResults;
  }

  -- Service Binding --
  Binding Type: OData V4 - UI
  Service URL:  /sap/opu/odata4/sap/z_inspection_api/srvd/sap/z_inspection_api/0001/
